### --- PAYMENTS ---
### Runs against the default fake provider (payment.provider=fake): no
### network, no account. Payment methods are Stripe's own test ids, so the
### same requests will work unchanged once the Stripe adapter exists:
###   pm_card_visa                                  succeeds
###   pm_card_visa_chargeDeclined                   fails, card_declined
###   pm_card_visa_chargeDeclinedInsufficientFunds  fails, insufficient_funds
###   pm_fake_provider_unavailable                  fake only: unreachable (503)
###
### Prerequisite: an OPEN invoice. Run billing.http through "Generate invoice
### — after the period closes" first; it sets {{billingInvoiceId}}.
### Every POST needs an Idempotency-Key header. {{$uuid}} generates a fresh
### one per request; requests meant to replay reuse a fixed value instead.
### Fixed keys are unique per tenant for the life of the database, so
### against a fresh invoice change them (e.g. success-attempt-2), or the
### first request returns 409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED.


### Auth — acme admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "email": "admin@acme.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("acmeToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Auth — demo admin, for the isolation checks
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "demo",
  "email": "admin@demo.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("demoToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Auth — acme support (read-only role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "email": "support@acme.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("supportToken", response.body.token);
%}


### Pay — missing Idempotency-Key (expects 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

### Pay — blank payment method (expects 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "paymentMethod": ""
}

### Pay — support role (expects 403 ACCESS_DENIED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{supportToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

### Pay — tenant isolation: acme's invoice under demo
### (expects 404 INVOICE_NOT_FOUND — must not leak or charge)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

### Pay — declined card (expects 201, status FAILED, failureCode card_declined;
### the invoice stays OPEN)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: declined-attempt-1

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa_chargeDeclined"
}

### Pay — same Idempotency-Key, different payment method
### (expects 409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: declined-attempt-1

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

### Pay — succeeding card (expects 201, status SUCCEEDED, Location header).
### Capture the payment id.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: success-attempt-1

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("paymentId", response.body.id);
%}

### Pay — replay with the same Idempotency-Key (expects 200, the same payment
### id as above, and no second payment row)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: success-attempt-1

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

### Pay — new key on an invoice that is now PAID (expects 409 INVOICE_NOT_PAYABLE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

### Invoice — expects status PAID and paidAt set
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### List payments for the invoice — expects FAILED then SUCCEEDED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### List payments — tenant isolation (expects 404 INVOICE_NOT_FOUND)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken}}

### Get payment by id — expects 200 SUCCEEDED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### Get payment by id — tenant isolation (expects 404 PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken}}

### Get payment — unknown id (expects 404 PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}


### --- Provider outage ---
### Needs a fresh OPEN invoice: re-run billing.http's setup for a new
### subscription and invoice first, so {{billingInvoiceId}} points at it.

### Pay — provider unavailable (expects 503 PAYMENT_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE;
### the payment is left PENDING because the outcome is unknown)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: outage-attempt-1

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_fake_provider_unavailable"
}

### Pay — another attempt while that one is PENDING
### (expects 409 PAYMENT_IN_PROGRESS — it must not reach the provider)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_card_visa"
}

### Pay — same key again: resubmits to the provider rather than replaying
### PENDING, so with the fake still "down" this is 503 again
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/invoices/{{billingInvoiceId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: outage-attempt-1

{
  "paymentMethod": "pm_fake_provider_unavailable"
}
